<title>USA: SmarTalk buys calling card company.</title>
<headline>SmarTalk buys calling card company.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>SmarTalk Teleservices Inc said on Sunday it has acquired privately held GTI Telecom Inc, a manufacturer and distributor of prepaid calling cards, for about $70 million.</p>
<p>The purchase price includes the issuance of about 2.5 million shares of common stock, $26 million of the company's subordinated notes due 2001 and the assumption of about $10 million of GTI's debt.</p>
<p>With the acquisition, SmarTalk adds more than 4,000 storefronts to its retail distribution network, which will now number 13,000 storefronts.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk, 212-859-1610</p>
